  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "4xx: Say Exactly What's Wrong",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Malformed vs Unauthenticated",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "400 Bad Request: unparseable JSON, missing field, bad syntax",
            "400 is the generic 4xx fallback",
            "401 Unauthorized actually means unauthenticated",
            "401 MUST name the scheme in `WWW-Authenticate:`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized",
            "WWW-Authenticate: Bearer realm=\"api\"",
            "# omit this and clients cannot recover"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "401 vs 403 In One Line",
          "text": "401 = who are you? 403 = I know who you are, and no. Re-authenticating never clears a 403."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Missing, Wrong Verb, Wrong Type",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "404 Not Found: no representation at this URL",
            "404 also hides a resource's existence from an unauthorized caller",
            "405 Method Not Allowed: URL exists, verb does not apply",
            "405 MUST send `Allow: GET, POST`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "406 Not Acceptable: nothing matches `Accept:`",
            "Rare — most servers just return their default format"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "State and Preconditions",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "409 Conflict: duplicate unique key, stale edit, parent with children",
            "410 Gone: intentionally and permanently removed",
            "410 beats 404 when you actually know the history",
            "412 Precondition Failed: `If-Match` guard broke — optimistic locking"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Trigger"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "413",
              "body too large"
            ],
            [
              "414",
              "URI too long"
            ],
            [
              "415",
              "wrong `Content-Type`"
            ],
            [
              "429",
              "rate limited"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "415 fires when you POST XML to a JSON-only endpoint",
            "422 Unprocessable Content: valid JSON, `age: -5`",
            "422 is the validation-error workhorse",
            "429 SHOULD carry `Retry-After: 60` and `RateLimit-*`"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "4xx: Say Exactly What's Wrong (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Pick One Convention",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "400 = I cannot parse this",
            "422 = I parsed it and the values are wrong",
            "Either reading is defensible — hold it API-wide"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Standard Error Body",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "json",
          "lines": [
            "{\"type\":\"/errors/bad-email\",",
            " \"title\":\"Invalid email\",",
            " \"status\":422, \"detail\":\"nope is not an email\",",
            " \"instance\":\"/users/42\"}"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "RFC 9457 `application/problem+json` is the standard shape",
            "Stop inventing a bespoke error envelope per service"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Which 5xx Means What",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Code",
            "Cause"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "500",
              "unhandled exception"
            ],
            [
              "502",
              "upstream sent garbage"
            ],
            [
              "503",
              "overloaded or deploying"
            ],
            [
              "504",
              "upstream ran out of clock"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "500 is your fault and not actionable by the client",
            "502: a proxy or load balancer got an invalid upstream response",
            "503 SHOULD include `Retry-After`",
            "504 differs from 502: the connection worked, time ran out"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Less Common, Still Real",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "501 Not Implemented: the server doesn't recognise the method at all",
            "501 is server-wide; 405 is per-resource",
            "505 HTTP Version Not Supported",
            "507 Insufficient Storage (WebDAV), 511 for captive portals"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Never Leak The Trace",
          "text": "No stack traces, SQL or file paths in a 5xx body. Return `{\"trace_id\":\"abc123\"}` and keep the rest in your logs."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Retry Discipline",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Retry 502, 503, 504 and connection errors",
            "Do NOT blindly retry 500 — the write may have committed",
            "Automatic retries only for idempotent methods",
            "POST needs an `Idempotency-Key` before any retry"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "5xx, Retries and Resilience",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "python",
          "lines": [
            "cap, base = 30, 0.2",
            "delay = random.uniform(0, min(cap, base * 2**n))",
            "# full jitter, not fixed interval"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Fixed-interval retries cause thundering herds",
            "Exponential backoff with full jitter spreads the load",
            "`Retry-After` overrides your calculation when present"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Circuit Breaker",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "closed",
              "N consecutive 5xx",
              "open: fail fast",
              "cooldown",
              "half-open probe"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "An open circuit fails fast and spares the dying upstream",
            "Half-open sends one probe before closing again"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Signals On The Wall",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "499 is nginx-only and non-standard",
            "It means the client hung up before your response",
            "Usually your endpoint is too slow, not an error"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "sidebox",
          "title": "Health Checks",
          "items": [
            "Return 200 only when dependencies actually answer",
            "A shallow `return 200` hides every real outage",
            "4xx rate is a client-contract signal",
            "5xx rate is a pager signal"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Decision Walk",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flowchart",
