        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Within 2xx: created something new → 201 + `Location`",
            "Queued for later → 202",
            "Nothing to return → 204",
            "Otherwise → 200"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Within 4xx: unparseable 400, not logged in 401",
            "Logged in but not allowed 403, no such URL 404",
            "Wrong verb 405, state clash 409",
            "Bad values 422, too fast 429"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Choosing the Right Code",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Flows End To End",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "http",
          "lines": [
            "POST /articles -> 201 Created",
            "Location: /articles/77",
            "# body = the created article"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`PUT /articles/77` with `If-Match` → 200 or 204",
            "200 when returning the entity, 204 when the client has it",
            "412 when the ETag is stale"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`DELETE /articles/77` → 204",
            "Repeat call → 404 or 410",
            "Blocked by dependents → 409"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Situation",
            "Answer"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "bad password",
              "401"
            ],
            [
              "too many attempts",
              "429 + `Retry-After`"
            ],
            [
              "malformed JSON",
              "400"
            ],
            [
              "`email: \"nope\"`",
              "422 + problem+json"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Async End To End",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "kind": "flow",
          "spec": {
            "nodes": [
              "POST /reports",
              "202 + /jobs/5",
              "GET /jobs/5",
              "200 running",
              "303 to /reports/91"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Four Ways To Get It Wrong",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "200 for everything with `success: false` — breaks monitoring and caches",
            "500 for validation errors — pages on-call for a user's typo",
            "401 when you meant 403 — clients loop re-authenticating forever",
            "302 after a POST when you meant 303 or 307 — body silently lost"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Before You Ship",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Assert the status code in tests, not just the body",
            "A route returning 200 instead of 201 breaks contracts silently"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "Code First, Then Words",
          "text": "The status code is the API's protocol-level answer; the body is the human-level detail. Get the code right, then explain in `problem+json`."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of HTTP FIELD MANUAL. Most APIs use about six status codes and get half of them wrong. This field manual walks every method and every status family — what safe, idempotent and cacheable actually mean, why 302 after a POST eats your form body, and the exact difference between 401 and 403, 400 and 422, 502 and 504. Ten pages of dense notes you can check a route against before you ship it.",
